1
00:00:00,394 --> 00:00:02,350
This was just checked with our server

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:03,244
switched off

3
00:00:03,244 --> 00:00:04,731
Nothing was contacted

4
00:00:05,725 --> 00:00:08,330
When one automated client reads

5
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:11,804
your site and hands what it found to another

6
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:14,795
all you can usually say is that the two

7
00:00:14,795 --> 00:00:16,006
look similar

8
00:00:17,064 --> 00:00:19,674
Canary Maze gives every automated

9
00:00:19,674 --> 00:00:21,654
visitor its own secret URL

10
00:00:21,654 --> 00:00:24,914
then records who else comes asking for it

11
00:00:24,914 --> 00:00:27,167
Every sentence on this page is computed

12
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:28,273
from the records

13
00:00:28,638 --> 00:00:31,769
A URL only context A was ever shown was

14
00:00:31,769 --> 00:00:33,913
requested by context B

15
00:00:33,913 --> 00:00:35,277
Different user agent

16
00:00:35,277 --> 00:00:36,713
different network

17
00:00:36,713 --> 00:00:38,692
This one is a seeded replay

18
00:00:38,692 --> 00:00:41,143
and the page says so itself

19
00:00:41,143 --> 00:00:43,372
The secret is that marked string

20
00:00:43,372 --> 00:00:45,751
there, in context B's request line

21
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,070
Now the part that matters

22
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:50,892
This recomputes every hash in your own browser

23
00:00:50,892 --> 00:00:52,420
from the bundle alone

24
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:53,620
Verified

25
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:55,725
Five hashes, with crypto.subtle

26
00:00:55,725 --> 00:00:58,142
and no request to our server at all

27
00:00:58,515 --> 00:01:00,490
So let's lie to it

28
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:03,468
We change the organic sighting count

29
00:01:03,468 --> 00:01:05,006
this page displays

30
00:01:05,006 --> 00:01:07,119
from zero to four thousand

31
00:01:07,119 --> 00:01:08,711
and press it again

32
00:01:10,916 --> 00:01:11,671
Caught

33
00:01:11,671 --> 00:01:15,009
The bundle commits to what the page shows

34
00:01:15,009 --> 00:01:17,296
not only to what it hashes

35
00:01:17,296 --> 00:01:20,164
An earlier build of this got that wrong

36
00:01:20,164 --> 00:01:22,913
and an independent review found it

37
00:01:23,857 --> 00:01:26,594
A sighting shows a secret moved between

38
00:01:26,594 --> 00:01:27,682
two contexts

39
00:01:27,682 --> 00:01:29,857
Not that there are two operators

40
00:01:29,857 --> 00:01:31,002
We measured that

41
00:01:31,002 --> 00:01:33,442
in the organizers' own public dump

42
00:01:34,637 --> 00:01:37,037
And the counters it will not inflate

43
00:01:37,037 --> 00:01:38,814
Organic sightings

44
00:01:38,814 --> 00:01:41,037
zero, reported as zero

45
00:01:41,037 --> 00:01:42,821
Humans are turned away by the gate

46
00:01:42,821 --> 00:01:44,691
and never enter the ledger at all

47
00:01:45,649 --> 00:01:46,949
Canary Maze

48
00:01:46,949 --> 00:01:48,796
The record checks out without trusting

49
00:01:48,796 --> 00:01:49,562
the recorder

